  "limitations": [
    "Manufacturer K122 cover STL retained at native millimetre scale; no complete populated PCB CAD was verified.",
    "Black PCB backside uses exact C3U source photograph; covered component side stays UNKNOWN. Photo pixels do not verify board layout, stack-up or electrical behavior.",
    "Board outline, pin holes and visible USB/antenna shapes are photograph-derived estimates. Native back crop301x513px, uncalibrated lighting/material colors.",
    "Single M2x4 countersunk screw is officially specified. Visible head/standoff dimensions estimated; hidden threads and insert retention unknown.",
    "Cover20x34x4.5mm versus official assembled20x34x4.6mm retained, no rescaling or physical measurements.",
    "Official K122 LCEDA component could not be fetched. Companion C122-B PCB link points to C3 directory, not accepted as populated C3U CAD. K122 GPIO22 listing conflicts with its visible label/schematic GPIO20; runtime uses separately audited pin map.",
    "K122 is a kit with one Stamp-C3U plus loose male/female headers, two HY2.0 sockets and a hex key. None are inferred to be soldered into the module.",
    "RGB package position is visible near[0,-5.6] under the covered flexure slot, but paper light transmission is unverified. No emissive paper decal or surface LED is invented."
  ],
